     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi everyone,</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to Lavaan and having trouble getting the models right for some ecological data.</div><div>The data are definitely spatially dependent and non-linear, so I thought I would try a new method </div><div>that adjusts for spatial autocorrelation.</div><div><br></div><div>But when trying to generate residuals from the model of type &quot;casewise&quot; as part of that process, </div><div>I see all the residuals are zero. Is that a sign that the model is completely wrong? EG:</div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">as.data.frame(residuals(model, &quot;casewise&quot;))</font></div><div><br></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"266\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:200pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"14\" style=\"width:11pt\">\r\n <col width=\"71\" style=\"width:53pt\">\r\n <col width=\"40\" style=\"width:30pt\">\r\n <col width=\"68\" style=\"width:51pt\">\r\n <col width=\"35\" style=\"width:26pt\">\r\n <col width=\"38\" style=\"width:29pt\">\r\n </colgroup><tbody><tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" width=\"14\" style=\"height:15.0pt;width:11pt\"></td>\r\n  <td width=\"71\" style=\"width:53pt\">TOTAL_AV</td>\r\n  <td width=\"40\" style=\"width:30pt\"> AREA</td>\r\n  <td width=\"68\" style=\"width:51pt\">  RAIN_NW</td>\r\n  <td width=\"35\" style=\"width:26pt\"> RW2</td>\r\n  <td width=\"38\" style=\"width:29pt\"> RAIN</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">1</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">2</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" align=\"right\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">3</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m most interested in the relationship between TOTAL_AV and RAIN_NW. The model looks like this:</div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">&#39;TOTAL_AV ~ RAIN + AREA + RAIN_NW + RW2</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"> AREA        ~ RAIN</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"> RAIN_NW  ~ RAIN</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"> RW2          ~ RAIN_NW</font></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\"> AREA        ~ RAIN_NW&#39;</font></div><div> </div><div>I&#39;m running it like this:</div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#0000ff\">sem(model, data, fixed.x = FALSE, std.ov = TRUE, meanstructure = TRUE)</font></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Producing:</div><div> </div><div> lavaan (0.5-19) converged normally after  65 iterations</div><div><br></div><div>  Number of observations                           492</div><div><br></div><div>  Estimator                                                ML</div><div>  Minimum Function Test Statistic              120.572</div><div>  Degrees of freedom                                 2</div><div>  P-value (Chi-square)                                0.000</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div></div><div><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"515\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:387pt\">\r\n <colgroup><col width=\"95\" style=\"width:71pt\">\r\n <col width=\"23\" style=\"width:17pt\">\r\n <col width=\"95\" style=\"width:71pt\">\r\n <col width=\"47\" style=\"width:35pt\">\r\n <col width=\"42\" style=\"width:32pt\">\r\n <col width=\"49\" span=\"2\" style=\"width:37pt\">\r\n <col