/tr>\r\n \r\n <tr height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">\r\n  <td height=\"20\" style=\"height:15.0pt\">RW2</td>\r\n  <td>r2</td>\r\n  <td>RW2</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\">0.901</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n  <td>NA</td>\r\n </tr></tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div>  </div><div>I&#39;m attempting to deal with the non-linearity for TOTAL_AV vs. RAIN_NW using the RW2 term <br>(i.e. RAIN_NW squared), but this seems inadequate.</div><div><br></div><div>Given regular functions don&#39;t seem to describe the relationships ( pic attached) I&#39;m wondering if </div><div>SEMs are even a good idea with this sort of data? Perhaps I would need to transform the variables, </div><div>but hopefully not as interpretation would be difficult.</div><div><br></div><div>          <a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-jv_5eE-7WLM/VpXyqt5RYkI/AAAAAAAABn0/cgZixu8nbTA/s1600/scatterplot.png\" style=\"text-align:center;margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-jv_5eE-7WLM/VpXyqt5RYkI/AAAAAAAABn0/cgZixu8nbTA/s1600/scatterplot.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792429076455000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UpKIDvOmVHqU1NEpBDEX-\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-jv_5eE-7WLM/VpXyqt5RYkI/AAAAAAAABn0/cgZixu8nbTA/s320/scatterplot.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\"></a></div><div><br></div><div>Sorry for rambling but I&#39;m pretty confused. Right now I don&#39;t think my use of lavaan is valid so any<br></div><div>hints would be greatly appreciated, thanks very much for designing the software!</div><div><br></div><div>Hugh</div></div>"
    ]
