     2,
     "On 01/13/2016 08:01 AM, Hugh Burley wrote:\r<br>&gt; But when trying to generate residuals from the model of type &quot;casewise&quot;\r<br>&gt; as part of that process,\r<br>&gt; I see all the residuals are zero. Is that a sign that the model is\r<br>&gt; completely wrong?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "No. It is a misunderstanding (mostly among ecologists for some reason), \r<br>about the nature of these &#39;residuals&#39;: these residuals are (in lavaan \r<br>0.5-20) not the same residuals as in regression models.\r<br>\r<br>See my comment about this here:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"https://github.com/yrosseel/lavaan/issues/44\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yrosseel/lavaan/issues/44&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792429076456000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PJ1DM9EePO5zd2nGoGtm1\">https://github.com/yrosseel/lavaan/issues/44</a>\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
